  <static seed="135" source="Library/Michigan/Chap16Sec3/Q01.pg">
    <statement><p>Find the triple integral of the function <m>f(x,y,z)</m>
over the region <m>W</m>, if
<m>f(x,y,z) = x^{2}+8y^{2}-z</m> and <m>W</m> is the rectangular box
<m>-1 \le x \le 0</m>, <m>2 \le y \le 4</m>,
<m>-1 \le z \le 0</m>.</p>
<p>triple integral = <fillin characters="55" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{1}{6}\mathopen{}\left(0--1\right)\mathopen{}\left(4-2\right)\mathopen{}\left(0--1\right)\mathopen{}\left(2\cdot \left(-1\cdot \left(-1\right)+-1\cdot 0+0\cdot 0\right)+2\cdot 8\cdot \left(2\cdot 2+2\cdot 4+4\cdot 4\right)+3\cdot \left(-1\right)\mathopen{}\left(0+-1\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\int_W f\,dV = \int_{-1}^{0} \int_{2}^{4} \int_{-1}^{0}
    (x^{2}+8y^{2}-z)\,dz\,dy\,dx =
\int_{-1}^{0} \int_{2}^{4}
    (x^2 + 8 y^2)z - \frac12 z^2)\bigg|_{-1}^{0}\,dy\,dx</me>
<me>= \int_{-1}^{0} \int_{2}^{4} (x^2 + 8 y^2)() -
    \frac12(-1)\,dy\,dx
 = \int_{-1}^{0} \int_{2}^{4} (x^2 + 8 y^2 - \frac{-1}{2})\,dy\,dx</me>
<me>= \int_{-1}^{0} (x^2 y + \frac{8}{3} y^3 - \frac{-1}{2} y)\bigg|_{2}^{4}\,dx
 = \int_{-1}^{0} (x^2 (2) + \frac{8}{3} (56) - \frac{-1}{2} (2)\,dx</me>
<me>= \int_{-1}^{0} (2 x^2 + \frac{448}{3}  + 1)\,dx
 = ( \frac{2}{3} x^3 + \frac{451}{3} x)\bigg|_{-1}^{0}</me>
<me>= 3(\frac{2}{3}(1) + \frac{451}{3} (1)) = 151.</me>



</solution>
